**What is this feature?**

This PR fixes an issue where provisioning API accepts a malformed template having extra text outside of definition block and template name matching definition name.

This occurs because the extra text outside of the definition block makes the GO template parser wrap the entire thing in a second definition block that uses the name of the template. If the name of the template matches the name of your definition block, this will create a duplicate definition.

Maybe in the future we'll want to just remove any extra text outside of definition blocks, but for now this will at least make sure the API does not mistakenly accept a malformed template.

**Special notes for your reviewer**:

Example templates to test this with:

**This is valid**:
Name: Alert Instance Template
```
{{ define "Alert Instance Template" }}
Firing: {{ .Labels.alertname }}
Silence: {{ .SilenceURL }}
{{ end }}
```
**This is valid**:
Name: Some other name
```
{{ define "Alert Instance Template" }}
Firing: {{ .Labels.alertname }}
Silence: {{ .SilenceURL }}
{{ end }} Extra Text
```

**This is invalid**
Name: Same name
```
{{ define "Same name" }}
Firing: {{ .Labels.alertname }}
Silence: {{ .SilenceURL }}
{{ end }} Extra Text
```

